** AUTHORED TEMPLATE — amplifier/ac_cm_reg (CM-loop health, frequency domain).
** Closed-loop COMMON-MODE output impedance: a unit AC common-mode current (0.5 A per
** side) is injected into both outputs; vocm/(1 A) = |Zcm(f)|. The CM feedback loop
** suppresses Zcm in-band, so:
**   zcm_lf_ohm     low-frequency Zcm — the CM stiffness the servo achieves
**   zcm_peak_ohm   the sweep maximum
**   cm_peaking_db  20*log10(peak/lf) — impedance peaking; a large value flags an
**                  underdamped CM loop (the external signature of poor CM phase margin)
** HONESTY NOTE: the internal CM loop gain/phase (T_cm, PM_cm) cannot be probed from a
** bench without breaking the loop inside the DUT — that is a composition-time
** measurement (insert a VIPRB/stb probe in the CMFB path of a composed variant). This
** bench measures the closed-loop observables that T_cm determines.
**
** Assumes a self-biased, differential-output DUT with a CM control loop:
**   .subckt <id> vinp vinn voutp voutn vdd vss
** Required bindings: DUT PORT_LINE VDD VCM CL FSTART FSTOP PPD PDK_INCLUDE.
.lib tsmc_n65_models.scs tt
.temp 27

.param VDD=1.5
.param VCM=0.8
.param CL=50f

Vdd  vdd 0 dc {VDD}
Vss  vss 0 dc 0
CLoadp voutp 0 {CL}
CLoadn voutn 0 {CL}
Vcm  vcm 0 dc {VCM}
Vinp vinp vcm dc 0
Vinn vinn vcm dc 0
* unit common-mode current injection (0.5 A AC per side -> 1 A total CM)
Icmp 0 voutp dc 0 ac 0.5
Icmn 0 voutn dc 0 ac 0.5

XDUT vinp vinn voutp voutn vdd vss amp_020_two_stage_miller_cmfb

.control
  set filetype=ascii
  ac dec 41 100 1G
  let zcm = mag((v(voutp)+v(voutn))/2)
  meas ac zcm_lf_ohm FIND zcm AT=100
  meas ac zcm_pk MAX zcm
  * MAX meas lines carry an `at=` suffix the result parser skips - re-print clean
  let zcm_peak_ohm = zcm_pk
  let cm_peaking_db = 20*log10(zcm_pk/zcm_lf_ohm)
  print zcm_peak_ohm cm_peaking_db
  write
  quit
.endc
.param x_dut_xm1_w=2u
.param x_dut_xm1_l=0.5u
.param x_dut_xm3_w=2u
